{"hw":"εἶἑν","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">εἶἑν</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">εἶἑν</span> (for the aspiration, found in cod. Rav. of <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> </span>, etc., cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.D.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Synt.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">319.26</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">An.Bachm.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.208</span> </span>), Particle used in dialogue and oratory, in passing to the next point, <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">well, quite so, very good</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Nu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1075</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ap.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">19a</span> </span>, etc.; \" <span class=\"gk\">εἶἑν\" ἐρῶ καὶ κατανεύσομαι καὶ ἀνανεύσομαι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">R.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">35o</span> </span> e: folld. by a question, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Nu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">176</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"gk\">εἶἑν: τί δῆτα</span>..; <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ph.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1308</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">εἶἑν: καὶ δὴ τεθνᾶσι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Med.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">386</span> </span>: folld. by imper., <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">El.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">534</span> </span>; in argument, <b class=\"lex-tr\">so far so good</b>: <span class=\"gk\">εἶἑν, ἐρεῖ δέ</span>.. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Antipho</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.2.3</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">εἶἑν, τοῦτο μὲν ἡμῖν κείσθω: ἔφαμεν δέ</span>.. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">R.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">350d</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">εἶἑν, ἀλλὰ νὴ Δία</span>.. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">20.75</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.</span> </span> Chr.<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">17.19</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"gk\">εἶἑν δή</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Smp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">213e</span> </span>. [At the beginning of a trimeter, <span class=\"gk\">εἶἑν, ἀκούω</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ch.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">657</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pax</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">663</span> </span>: extra versum in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> </span> l.c.]</div></div>"}